---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} handles preferences, alarms, analytics configuration, and browser permissions.`}
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language policy</p><h1>Privacy</h1><p>
      {siteConfig.name} does not require an account. Clock preferences, saved timer presets, converter
      zones, alarms, and world-clock locations are stored in your browser using local storage. They are
      not synchronized between devices. Running countdowns use session storage for this tab and survive
      a refresh. Your browser may restore that tab data when restoring a browsing session.
    </p><h2>Network requests</h2><p>
      The tools calculate time in your browser. This build sends no analytics events and loads no
      advertising scripts. The hosting provider receives normal page requests, which can include
      your IP address and requested URL. Timer and converter links can contain the duration, time
      zones and dates you choose; anyone you give a link to can read those values.
    </p><h2>Offline pages</h2><p>
      Previously visited pages and their assets can be cached by a service worker. Clearing site
      data removes those cached files as well as your saved settings.
    </p><h2>Permissions</h2><p>
      Notification and screen wake-lock permissions are requested only after you choose the relevant
      control. You can revoke them in browser settings. Alarm labels are included in local
      notifications but are not uploaded by the core app.
    </p><h2>Data removal</h2><p>
      Delete individual alarms or locations in the app, or clear this site’s storage in your browser
      to remove all saved preferences.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
